OL,3,GNEWSAFamily 'traumatised' after tree
OL,4,Afalls into garden
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man says his family were "left
OL,7,Ftraumatised" after a tree fell into his
OL,8,Fgarden, narrowly missing his home.
OL,10,FJerry Onyeri said the tree, which stood
OL,11,Fon a strip of land owned by Barratt
OL,12,FHomes, "crashed" through a fence into
OL,13,Fhis garden in North Hykeham, near
OL,14,FLincoln, during Storm Boelo on 25
OL,15,FOctober.
OL,17,FA neighbour said they reported concerns
OL,18,Fabout the tree to FirstPort, a property
OL,19,Fmanagement firm that maintains parts of
OL,20,Fthe Barratt development, months before
OL,21,Fit fell.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,387,380,200,160,0,100
